        "id": 33776,
        "name": "flamethrower49",
        "username": "flamethrower49",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/f/838e76/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2012-06-24T05:30:44.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"&quot;&quot;Reckless&quot;&quot;\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n \"\"Reckless\"\":</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>How do you manage to have short, victorious games against the Matriarch!?  My group and I find her to be frustrating mechanically and thematically, and just don’t have much fun against her in general.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Thus far, I’ve found that you beat the Matriarch quickly, or you don’t beat her.  That particular game was the result of McBehrer’s Twist the Ether/Absolute Zero/Coolant Blast combo ™, that harmlessly channeled 60 fire damage through AZ, then released it at the Matriarch.  It was kinda lucky that all the pieces came together so quickly.</p>\n<p>I don’t usually set her up, myself.</p>",
        "post_number": 4,
